Social Media Application Architecture
Let's design a simple social-media application like a basic version of Instagram, Facebook, or X.

The core idea is:

Users
  ↓
Frontend
  ↓
Backend API
  ↓
Business Logic
  ↓
Database + Storage

=============================



2. Component-by-Component Architecture

Component 1: Authentication

Responsibility

Controls who can access the application.


Features



Register


Login


Logout


Password hashing


Session/token management


Password reset
================================


Component 2: User Profiles

Each user has a profile.


Features



Profile picture


Username


Biography


Followers


Following


User posts

=====================================


Component 3: Posts

This is the core content system.


Users can:




Create posts


Edit posts


Delete posts


View posts

====================================


Component 5: Feed
The feed determines which posts a user sees.



For a simple MVP:


User follows people
        ↓
Get followed user IDs
        ↓
Get their recent posts
        ↓
Sort by newest
        ↓
Display feed



====================================


Component 6: Likes

Users can like posts.



Like
├── id
├── user_id
├── post_id
└── created_at

===================================


Component 7: Comments

Users can comment on posts.


Comment
├── id
├── post_id
├── user_id
├── content
└── created_at
======================================



Component 8: Follow System

Users follow other users.


Use a relationship table:


Follow
├── follower_id
├── following_id
└── created_at
=====================================
Component 9: Notifications
Examples:


Someone liked your post.


Someone commented.


Someone followed you.
=====================================
